{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>ויולך</b> Four times in the Masorah: ויולך ה' את הים · ויולך אותם שמרונה — by Elisha, when he struck the servants of the king of Aram with blindness (סנורים), to teach that the Egyptians too were struck with blindness (סנורים); and the other: ויוקח אותם נבוזראדן וגו' ויולך אותם אל מלך בבל; and the other, regarding the remnant of the exile (according to one opinion they are counted as one, for it is one matter); and the other: ויולך חושך ולא אור — for their eyes were darkened from the exile as though they had been struck with blindness (סנורים)." "<b>ברוח קדים</b> Two times in the Masorah: here and the other: ברוח קדים תשבר אניות תרשיש. This teaches that all the ships of the sea were shattered when the sea split."], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {0 "The comment cites four occurrences of ויולך in the Masorah but lists the second occurrence with the verb form ויוקח rather than ויולך; the juxtaposition-reading depends on the third occurrence (Genesis 31:34, שארית הגולה) being counted as one with another, following one opinion that they share a single theme."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:12:57.599805833Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}